# Android Work Profile Setup – End User Guide

## Objective
Set up your Android device to securely access company apps and enable contact sync for caller ID and search.

---

## 1. Install Company Portal

- Open Google Play Store
- Install: Company Portal

---

## 2. Sign in

- Open Company Portal
- Sign in with your work account

---

## 3. Start setup

- Tap:
  Enroll device / Begin setup

- Follow instructions

---

## 4. Work Profile is created

During setup:

- A Work Profile is created on your device
- You will see:
  - Apps with a briefcase icon
  - Separate "Work" app section

---

## 5. Install apps

In Company Portal install:

- Microsoft Outlook
- Microsoft Teams
- Microsoft OneDrive

Apps will be installed inside the Work Profile

---

## 6. Open Outlook

- Sign in with your work account
- Follow prompts

You will be asked to:
- Set a PIN
- Allow Contacts permission (IMPORTANT)

---

## 7. Contacts Sync (IMPORTANT)

For contacts to work:

1. Allow Contacts access when prompted
2. Ensure Outlook setting:
   Save Contacts = ON

---

## 8. How contacts are used on Android (important behavior)

Once enabled:

### Caller identification
- Incoming calls will show names from your work contacts
- Even when using your personal dialer

---

### Contact search
- You can search work contacts in:
  - Phone dialer
  - Contacts app
  - Messaging apps

---

### Important technical behavior

- Contacts are NOT copied to your personal profile
- Contacts remain in the Work Profile
- Android allows secure cross-profile lookup

---

## 9. Start working

You can now:

- Use Outlook (email + calendar)
- Join meetings in Teams
- Access files in OneDrive

---

## Important Notes

✅ Your personal apps and data remain unchanged  
✅ Work data is stored in the Work Profile  
✅ Only work apps are managed by your organization  

---

## Key Difference vs iPhone

- Android: contacts are securely shared for search/caller ID  
- iPhone: contacts are copied directly to device  
